# Oriana UI/UX — always on

Before designing or changing any public UI, read and apply these project skills (in order):

1. `oriana-modern-ui` — brand tokens, layout, motion, component placement
2. `frontend-design` — distinctive, non-generic visual direction
3. `ui-ux-pro-max` — layout, typography, interaction, responsive patterns
4. `web-design-guidelines` — Vercel Web Interface Guidelines review
5. `accessibility` — WCAG 2.2 keyboard, contrast, semantics
6. `vercel-react-best-practices` — Next.js/React performance while building UI

## Non-negotiables

- Preserve Oriana brand tokens (`oriana-navy`, `oriana-blue`, `oriana-sky`, `oriana-sun`, `oriana-silver`, `oriana-muted`, `oriana-surface`). Do not invent a purple/indigo or cream/terracotta AI-default theme.
- Public UI lives in `apps/ui`; pages/routing stay in `apps/cms`. Prefer extending existing `apps/ui/src/components/oriana/*` over one-off page markup.
- One job per section: one headline, one short supporting line, clear CTA when needed.
- Heroes are full-bleed compositions (brand + headline + short support + CTA + dominant media). No card grids, stat strips, or floating badges in the first viewport.
- Motion: use existing `FadeIn` / Framer Motion patterns; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Content comes from Payload when available; never hardcode fake CMS copy that fights production content.
- Desktop + mobile both required; no hover-only critical actions.
